{#
  The recipe view (FSD §8.2, §9) — one to three recipes side by side as a
  cooking sheet, with ingredients and directions.

  **Every measurement here comes from the approved mockup**
  (`mockups/preview/09-wand-rezepte.png`, generated by
  `tools/mockup-gen/pages_wand.py`), and the numbers are the ones that file
  uses, not new ones:

    title     32 px bold in Spectra blue at the column top, advance 46 px per
              wrapped line (the mockup's 40 px black cost three lines on a real
              recipe name; blue is [zur Ansicht], green was the step before)
    meta      26 px in #555555, advance 48 px, with **blue** marks — a 2 px
              stroke in grey dithers into a speckle (measured)
    rule      3 px Spectra blue under the head, 24 px of air below it
    heading   32 px bold in Spectra green (#1e8c46), block height 52 px —
              no underline: the rule under the head is the only one
    body      28 / 26 / 24 px, line advance 40 / 37 / 34
    direction 22 px / 31 px when the alternative is cutting — the one place
              this page goes past FSD §7's floor, and only for the directions
    gutter    a 2 px **black** rule down the middle of the 40 px gap — the
              mockup's #aaaaaa dithered into a dotted trail (measured)
    bullets   ingredients are "· " per item
    emphasis  Paprika's **markers** become bold runs, one element per line

  The type size and the sub-column count arrive decided from
  `recipe_layout.py`. Nothing is computed here on purpose: the height model and
  the drawing have to be the same thing, and the first version of this page —
  where CSS wrapped what Python had budgeted in characters — ran off the bottom
  of the canvas and was clipped without a word.

  **The whole canvas is used, whatever the number of recipes**
  [Festlegung 2026-08-22]: two share it half and half, one gets all of it. The
  width and the number of sub-columns arrive from `recipe_layout.py` — one
  recipe flows its body in three columns of 773 px rather than setting a single
  line 160 characters wide (FSD §7), which no type size makes returnable at
  cooking distance.

  Layout follows FSD §7: no rule thinner than 2 px, no gradient. `pre-wrap`
  for the directions: they are multi-line free text at Paprika [belegt].
#}{#
  The marks of the meta line. Inline SVG rather than characters or emoji: the
  add-on image carries DejaVu Sans and nothing else, an emoji font would not be
  there to fall back on, and a colour emoji is the last thing to hand a
  six-colour panel. Drawn at a 24-unit grid with 2-unit strokes, which is ~2 px
  at the 26 px this line is set in — the minimum FSD §7 allows for a line.
#}
{%- macro mark(kind) -%}
  {%- if kind == "servings" -%}
    <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3.5"/></svg>
  {%- elif kind == "prep" -%}
    <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M6 3v8a3 3 0 0 0 6 0V3"/><path d="M9 11v10"/><path d="M18 3c-1.5 2-2 4-2 6s.5 3 2 3v9"/></svg>
  {%- elif kind == "cook" -%}
    <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M2 9h20"/><path d="M4.5 9v8a3 3 0 0 0 3 3h9a3 3 0 0 0 3-3V9"/><path d="M9 5.5c0-1 1-1.5 1-2.5M14 5.5c0-1 1-1.5 1-2.5"/></svg>
  {%- elif kind == "time" -%}
    <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M12 6.5V12l3.5 2.5"/></svg>
  {%- else -%}
    <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><rect x="3" y="14" width="4.5" height="7" rx="1"/><rect x="9.75" y="9" width="4.5" height="12" rx="1"/><rect x="16.5" y="4" width="4.5" height="17" rx="1"/></svg>
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endmacro -%}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="{{ language }}">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <title>ePaperEngine</title>
    <style>
      html,
      body {
        margin: 0;
        padding: 0;
        width: 2560px;
        height: 1440px;
        overflow: hidden;
        background: #fff;
        color: #000;
        font-family: "DejaVu Sans", sans-serif;
      }
      main {
        box-sizing: border-box;
        width: 2560px;
        height: 1440px;
        padding: 80px;
        display: flex;
        gap: 40px;
        justify-content: center;
        align-items: stretch;
      }
      .column {
        flex: none;
        position: relative;
      }
      /* The clip lives on the inner box, not on the column: the separator is an
         absolutely positioned child at a negative offset, and `overflow: hidden`
         on the column would cut off the very rule it is meant to carry. It stays
         as a safety net — if the height model in recipe_layout.py is ever off,
         a column should stop at its own edge rather than run into the next. */
      .inner {
        height: 100%;
        overflow: hidden;
      }
      /* The separator sits in the middle of the 40 px gutter. The mockup draws
         it 2 px in #aaaaaa; **grey does not survive the panel**. Measured on the
         first real render: dithered against the six Spectra primaries, that line
         came out as 67 % black pixels in one column and 33 % in the next — a
         dotted trail, not a rule. FSD §7 allows grey as an *area* down to 170,
         and this is the reading of it for a hairline. Black at 2 px keeps the
         mockup's intent (lighter than the 3 px rule under the head) and is the
         only way to get an unbroken line. */
      .column + .column::before {
        content: "";
        position: absolute;
        left: -21px;
        top: 0;
        bottom: 0;
        width: 2px;
        background: #000;
      }
      .title {
        /* 32 px, not the mockup's 40 [Festlegung 2026-08-22]: a real recipe
           name — "Blumenkohl aus der Tajine mit gehobeltem Trüffel und
           Erbsenmousseline", 69 characters — was three lines and 168 px of a
           1.280 px column at 40 px, before a word of recipe.
           **These two numbers are load-bearing:** recipe_layout.TITLE_PX and
           TITLE_LINE measure the head with them, and a page that sets something
           else here silently mis-measures every column. */
        font-size: 32px;
        font-weight: bold;
        line-height: 46px;
        /* Spectra blue [zur Ansicht 2026-08-22]. Like the green of the section
           headings it is a palette primary, so it carries no dither raster of
           its own — only the fringe every glyph edge has (FSD §15). */
        color: #1e3cb4;
      }
      .meta {
        font-size: 26px;
        line-height: 48px;
        color: #555555;
        display: flex;
        flex-wrap: wrap;
        align-items: center;
        gap: 0 10px;
      }
      .meta .sep {
        color: #555555;
      }
      .meta svg {
        /* **Blue, not grey.** The marks are 2 px strokes, and a 2 px stroke in
           #aaaaaa was measured coming off this panel as 67 % black pixels in one
           column and 33 % in the next — a speckle, not a line. Blue is a Spectra
           primary and comes out solid, and it ties the marks to the title and
           the rule. The *text* stays the mockup's grey. */
        width: 1em;
        height: 1em;
        vertical-align: -0.12em;
        color: #1e3cb4;
        flex: none;
      }
      .meta .part {
        display: inline-flex;
        align-items: center;
        gap: 8px;
        white-space: nowrap;
      }
      .rule {
        height: 3px;
        /* Spectra blue with the title [Festlegung 2026-08-22]. */
        background: #1e3cb4;
        margin-bottom: 24px;
      }
      .heading {
        font-size: 32px;
        font-weight: bold;
        color: #1e8c46;
        height: 52px;
        line-height: 32px;
      }
      .body {
        /* The two headings travel inside this flow, so a single recipe reads
           down column one and on into column two — the height model counts
           them as lines for the same reason. */
        column-gap: 40px;
      }
      .heading,
      .group {
        /* A heading at the foot of a sub-column with its list in the next one
           is the one break this layout must not make. */
        break-inside: avoid;
        break-after: avoid;
      }
      .group {
        margin-bottom: 20px;
      }
      .item {
        /* An empty source line is a group break in the ingredient list, and it
           keeps its line rather than collapsing — the height model counted it. */
        min-height: 1px;
      }
      .directions {
        /* The directions may be set one step below the column — the only place
           in this page that goes past FSD §7's 24 px floor, and only when the
           alternative is cutting text. Both numbers come from the model
           (recipe_layout.CRAMPED_PX / CRAMPED_LINE) so the height it measured
           is the height that gets set. */
      }
      .dline {
        /* One element per source line: the line breaks in Paprika's free text
           are the only structure it has, and they have to survive. An empty
           line keeps its height — the model counted it. */
        min-height: 1px;
      }
      .dline b {
        font-weight: bold;
      }
      .cut {
        margin-top: 20px;
        color: #dc1e1e;
        font-weight: bold;
        font-size: 26px;
      }
      .empty {
        margin: auto;
        font-size: 56px;
        text-align: center;
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      {% if not columns %}
        {# Reachable by pinning the recipe view with nothing selected. A legible
           sentence beats an empty white wall, and beats a failure — nothing is
           broken, there is simply nothing to cook. #}
        <div class="empty">{{ t("recipes.empty") }}</div>
      {% endif %}
      {% for column in columns %}
        <div class="column" style="width: {{ column.width }}px; font-size: {{ column.font_px }}px; line-height: {{ column.line_px }}px">
         <div class="inner">
          <div class="title">{{ column.name }}</div>
          {% if column.meta_parts %}
            <div class="meta">
              {% for part in column.meta_parts %}
                {% if not loop.first %}<span class="sep">·</span>{% endif %}
                <span class="part">{{ mark(part.icon) }}{{ part.text }}</span>
              {% endfor %}
            </div>
          {% endif %}
          <div class="rule"></div>
          <div class="body" style="column-count: {{ column.body_columns }}">
          {% if column.ingredients %}
            <div class="heading">{{ t("recipes.ingredients") }}</div>
            <div class="group" style="column-count: {{ column.ingredient_columns }}; column-gap: 24px">
              {% for item in column.ingredients %}
                <div class="item">{% if item %}· {{ item }}{% endif %}</div>
              {% endfor %}
            </div>
          {% endif %}
          {% if column.directions %}
            <div class="heading">{{ t("recipes.directions") }}</div>
            <div class="directions" style="font-size: {{ column.directions_px }}px; line-height: {{ column.directions_line }}px">
            {% for line in column.direction_lines %}
              <div class="dline">{% for run in line %}{% if run.bold %}<b>{{ run.text }}</b>{% else %}{{ run.text }}{% endif %}{% endfor %}</div>
            {% endfor %}
            </div>
          {% endif %}
          </div>
          {% if column.truncated %}
            <div class="cut">{{ t("recipes.truncated") }}</div>
          {% endif %}
         </div>
        </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
